# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#  Pantessa — environment template.
#
#      cp .env.example .env.local
#
#  PLACEHOLDERS ONLY — never commit a real secret. `.env` and `.env*.local` are
#  gitignored; this file is not.
#
#  Two things bite everyone once:
#    • Prisma's CLI reads `.env`, NOT `.env.local`. Put DATABASE_URL in both, or
#      pass it inline on every prisma command.
#    • `NEXT_PUBLIC_*` values are inlined at BUILD time. Rebuild after changing
#      one — restarting the server is not enough.
#
#  What works with how little (mirrors the README's Environment section):
#    nothing but the code            the site builds; marketing + docs render
#    + DATABASE_URL, SESSION_SECRET  sign-in, chat persistence, intent links,
#                                    jobs, dashboard, the agent desk — the product
#    + ALCHEMY_API_KEY               multi-chain wallet scans, portfolio cards,
#                                    cross-chain funding plans
#    + a connected wallet            the whole native transaction layer:
#                                    build, guard, sign, receipt
#    + ANTHROPIC_API_KEY             the planner fallback for asks no gate claims
#
#  House rule for every venue key below: a MISSING key produces a named refusal
#  in the chat, not a crash. Nothing here is required for the app to boot.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────


# ── Database (Prisma / Postgres) — REQUIRED for anything stateful ────────────
# Chat persistence, intent links, creator pages, jobs, DCA schedules, guardians,
# the dashboard, the agent desk and the roster all reach Prisma DIRECTLY — they
# do not consult USE_DB. Without DATABASE_URL those surfaces fail; the marketing
# and docs pages still render.
#
# pgvector is REQUIRED: prisma/schema.prisma declares `extensions = [vector]`
# (semantic routing, `McpServer.embedding`), so `db:push` runs
# CREATE EXTENSION vector and FAILS on a Postgres that doesn't have it. Neon's
# free tier ships pgvector — use the POOLER host.
#
#   DATABASE_URL='postgresql://…' npx pnpm@8 db:push
#   DATABASE_URL='postgresql://…' npx pnpm@8 db:seed-free-mcps
DATABASE_URL=postgresql://user:pass@host/pantessa?sslmode=require

# USE_DB gates ONE thing: whether the MCP DIRECTORY and its satellites read
# Postgres. 'true' (+ DATABASE_URL) → the live directory, endpoint health,
# incidents, reputation scores, route traces and smart-endpoint auto-calling
# (lib/catalog.ts, lib/health.ts, lib/incidents.ts, lib/reputation.ts,
# lib/route-trace.ts, lib/route-telemetry.ts, /api/tools/stats).
# Unset/false → those fall back to the curated in-code catalog
# (lib/free-fleet.ts + lib/mcp-data.ts) and auto-calling says so out loud.
# It does NOT gate the product surfaces above.
USE_DB=true


# ── Sessions (SIWE) — REQUIRED for sign-in ───────────────────────────────────
# Signs the SIWE session JWT (lib/auth.ts) and the job capability tokens that
# let a chat turn advance its own job (lib/job-token.ts); also salts the
# unsigned-turn rate-limit hash (lib/turn-limits.ts). Must be ≥16 chars — it
# throws rather than degrading. Any long random string:  openssl rand -hex 32
SESSION_SECRET=change-me-to-a-long-random-string


# ── Canonical public origin ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The exact host that serves 200 — with www, no trailing slash, never a host
# that redirects. Feeds canonical/og:url, the sitemap, robots, the RSS feed,
# Stripe return URLs, and every absolute link handed to an agent
# (lib/site-url.ts). Getting it wrong is quiet, not loud: `fetch` DROPS the
# Authorization header across a cross-origin redirect.
# Defaults to https://www.pantessa.com when unset.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL=https://www.pantessa.com


# ── Planner fallback (Anthropic) ─────────────────────────────────────────────
# The native transaction gates are deterministic parsers, so building, guarding
# and signing need NO model key at all. This powers only the generic planner
# that catches asks no gate claims. Without it those asks answer honestly
# ("ANTHROPIC_API_KEY not set") instead of failing.
# The planner deliberately runs on the direct Anthropic API — never through a
# paid/metered inference engine.
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=sk-ant-YOUR_ANTHROPIC_API_KEY
# PLANNER_MODEL=claude-haiku-4-5-20251001    # default; also used by mcp:lint


# ── Wallet connectors (browser sign-in) ──────────────────────────────────────
# WalletConnect project id → the WalletConnect lane in the sign-in modal.
# Unset = the connector is hidden; injected wallets (MetaMask, Coinbase) still
# work. https://cloud.reown.com
NEXT_PUBLIC_WC_PROJECT_ID=YOUR_WALLETCONNECT_PROJECT_ID


# ── Coinbase CDP — embedded wallets, social sign-in, Spend Permissions ───────
# Server credentials. All three are needed to sign as a CDP server wallet
# (api-key id/secret alone cannot sign) — lib/cdp.ts fails closed and the
# expense-account/Spend-Permission routes degrade instead of erroring.
# CDP Portal → API Keys: https://portal.cdp.coinbase.com
CDP_API_KEY_ID=YOUR_CDP_API_KEY_ID
CDP_API_KEY_SECRET=YOUR_CDP_API_KEY_SECRET
CDP_WALLET_SECRET=YOUR_CDP_WALLET_SECRET
# Network for new Spend Permissions. Defaults to 'base-sepolia'; flip to
# mainnet once a Smart Account is funded (lib/cdp.ts).
# CDP_SPEND_NETWORK=base
#
# Client-side project id — required for the embedded wallet + email/social
# sign-in lanes in the sign-in modal (lib/cdp-embedded.ts). Public; allowlist
# your origin in the CDP portal. Unset = those lanes don't render.
NEXT_PUBLIC_CDP_PROJECT_ID=YOUR_CDP_PROJECT_ID
#
# Social sign-in (Google, Apple, X) runs through the CDP Embedded Wallet SDK:
# enable each provider and set its OAuth client id/secret + redirect URIs in
# the CDP Portal (Embedded Wallets → Sign-in methods), NOT here. The app only
# reads NEXT_PUBLIC_CDP_PROJECT_ID.

# On-ramp (card / Apple Pay / ACH → USDC on Base). Fails closed: the funding
# chip is offered only when this is exactly 'true' AND the CDP api-key pair
# above is present (lib/onramp.ts). Needs Onramp approved on the CDP project.
# ONRAMP_ENABLED=true


# ── Wallet + market reads ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Alchemy — one key covers Ethereum, Base, Arbitrum (+ the other chains in
# lib/alchemy.ts): priced holdings, recent transactions, the portfolio card,
# and the cross-chain funding scans. Without it those reads fall back to the
# keyless Base-only on-chain path — always works, just single-chain.
# https://dashboard.alchemy.com → API Keys
ALCHEMY_API_KEY=YOUR_ALCHEMY_API_KEY

# OpenSea — the whole NFT layer (gallery, transfers, Seaport sells/buys).
# Without it every NFT ask refuses BY NAME ("the NFT layer needs
# OPENSEA_API_KEY on the server") rather than guessing at what you own.
# https://docs.opensea.io/reference/api-keys
OPENSEA_API_KEY=YOUR_OPENSEA_API_KEY

# LiFi — optional. Sent as `x-lifi-api-key` on the LiFi venue/bridge quotes
# (lib/lifi-venue.ts). Quotes work keyless; a key raises the rate limit.
# LIFI_API_KEY=YOUR_LIFI_API_KEY

# Optional RPC overrides used when verifying a receipt on-chain
# (lib/receipt-verify.ts). Public RPCs are the default.
# BASE_RPC_URL=
# BASE_SEPOLIA_RPC_URL=

# Optional Snapshot hosts (governance reads + the vote relay). Defaults are
# hub.snapshot.org / seq.snapshot.org.
# SNAPSHOT_HUB_URL=
# SNAPSHOT_SEQUENCER_URL=

# Optional extra Base token lists (comma-separated URLs) merged into the
# resolver in lib/token-list.ts.
# TOKEN_LIST_URLS=


# ── Autonomy layer (crons) ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Vercel Cron sends `Authorization: Bearer ${CRON_SECRET}` to /api/cron/*.
# FAIL-CLOSED: with no secret set the cron routes are DISABLED (401), so jobs,
# DCA, the Hyperliquid + spot guardians and the roster manager never advance.
CRON_SECRET=change-me-to-a-long-random-string

# Encrypts the delegated Hyperliquid agent keys at rest — they are encrypted
# before they touch the DB and decrypted only inside the guardian run
# (lib/hl-guardian-store.ts). ≥16 chars; required to arm or run a Guardian.
GUARDIAN_KEY_SECRET=change-me-to-a-long-random-string

# HL_GUARDIAN_TESTNET=true   # point the guardian at Hyperliquid testnet


# ── Admin surfaces ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Comma-separated wallet addresses, added to the hardcoded OWNER_WALLETS in
# lib/admin.ts. Gates the admin dashboards (/dashboard/admin,
# /dashboard/failures, the treasury + cohort views) and the blog editor.
# Server routes enforce it; the client check only shows/hides the nav chip.
# ADMIN_WALLETS=0xYOUR_ADMIN_WALLET,0xANOTHER

# Vercel Blob token — blog image uploads (/api/blog/upload). Without it the
# route answers that uploads are not configured.
# BLOB_READ_WRITE_TOKEN=


# ── Billing (Stripe) ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Optional locally. Without the secret key, /api/billing/plan reports
# stripeConfigured:false and checkout is unavailable; plans still render.
# The webhook secret verifies the signature on /api/billing/webhook.
# STRIPE_SECRET_KEY=sk_test_YOUR_STRIPE_SECRET_KEY
# STRIPE_WEBHOOK_SECRET=whsec_YOUR_STRIPE_WEBHOOK_SECRET


# ── Transactional email (Resend) ─────────────────────────────────────────────
# Best-effort by design: sending NEVER throws and never fails the caller, and
# the whole module no-ops when RESEND_API_KEY is unset (lib/email.ts).
# https://resend.com → API Keys
# RESEND_API_KEY=re_YOUR_RESEND_API_KEY
#
# Sender identity. Set BOTH to a domain you have verified in Resend
# (DKIM + SPF), or mail authenticates as someone else's domain and scores as
# spam. Pantessa's production mail still sends from the yeetful.com envelope
# on purpose — that is the domain currently verified in Resend; pantessa.com
# has no MX/SPF/DKIM yet.
# EMAIL_FROM="Pantessa <onboarding@your-verified-domain.com>"
# EMAIL_REPLY_TO=you@your-verified-domain.com


# ── Feature flags ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The agent desk (/api/broker — another agent opens an intent, hands it to its
# human to sign, hears back over a signed webhook). FAIL-CLOSED: the write/scan
# surface serves only when this is exactly 'true'. Existing intents can always
# be checked and closed (lib/broker-policy.ts).
# BROKER_DESK_ENABLED=true
# BROKER_MAX_INTENT_USD=500     # per-intent cap on the AGENT-SIGNED path
#
# Desk pricing, fail-closed to FREE (lib/broker-pricing.ts): setting a payment
# address flips the desk's value tools to x402-per-call. Unset = free.
# BROKER_PAYMENT_ADDRESS=0xYOUR_PAYMENT_ADDRESS
# BROKER_X402_PRICE_USD=0.02    # default
# BROKER_X402_NETWORK=base      # default

# The Roster (hire AI agents for your money) — in development, dark by default.
# FAIL-CLOSED on writes, except fire/unlist/decline, which are never walled.
# Both halves are needed: the server flag gates the API, the NEXT_PUBLIC one
# gates the UI (and is baked in at build time).
# ROSTER_ENABLED=true
# NEXT_PUBLIC_ROSTER_ENABLED=true
# NEXT_PUBLIC_ROSTER_HOMEPAGE=true   # flips the homepage to the Roster story
# ROSTER_MAX_CAP_USD=                # per-slot mandate cap ceiling
#
# The house manager's identity: any opaque string — its HASH is the agent's
# public handle (lib/roster-managers.ts). Unset → the storefront's house row
# reads "coming soon" and /api/cron/roster is a silent no-op.
# HOUSE_MANAGER_KEY=any-opaque-string


# ── Protocol fees ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Single source of truth in lib/fees.ts. Every override is validated and falls
# back to the pinned default rather than silently shipping a typo.
# YEETFUL_TREASURY=0xYOUR_TREASURY        # fee recipient; point staging at a burner
# YEETFUL_SWAP_FEE_BPS=20                 # base swap fee, clamped [0,100]
# YEETFUL_LINK_SWAP_FEE_BPS=50            # link-attributed tier, clamped [0,100]
#
# The Hyperliquid perp builder fee, in TENTHS of a basis point — 100 is the
# venue cap (10bps); 0 disables it and no builder field rides the order. The
# builder account must hold ≥100 USDC of HL perps account value before the
# venue will pay it, and until then guarded perp builds REFUSE — set 0 to ship
# without the fee.
# YEETFUL_HL_BUILDER_FEE_TENTH_BPS=100


# ── x402 agent wallet (server-paid MCP calls) ────────────────────────────────
# Third-party x402 endpoints are CORS-locked, so payment happens server-side.
# This wallet signs those payments in USDC on Base (lib/agent-wallet.ts).
#
# ⚠ A FUNDED BURNER ONLY. Chat turns can spend from it. Never a wallet holding
# real funds. Without it, paid MCP calls are simply unavailable — the free
# fleet and the whole native transaction layer are unaffected.
# PRIVATE_KEY=0xYOUR_BURNER_PRIVATE_KEY


# ── Optional / local development ─────────────────────────────────────────────
# Semantic routing embeddings (lib/embeddings.ts → lib/retrieval.ts, written by
# `db:embed`). Unset → retrieval falls back to keyword matching.
# OPENAI_API_KEY=sk-YOUR_OPENAI_API_KEY

# Point a free MCP at a local dev server instead of its *.yeetful.com host.
# FREE_MCP_URL_OVERRIDES={"uniswap-free":"http://localhost:3261/mcp"}
# FREE_UNISWAP_MCP_BASE, FREE_COW_MCP_BASE, FREE_AAVE_MCP_BASE,
# FREE_LIDO_MCP_BASE, FREE_MORPHO_MCP_BASE, FREE_HYPERLIQUID_MCP_BASE,
# FREE_OPENSEA_MCP_BASE, FREE_NEAR_INTENTS_MCP_BASE, FREE_SNAPSHOT_MCP_BASE,
# FREE_ROBINHOOD_MCP_BASE, FREE_WALLET_MCP_BASE, FREE_FUNDING_MCP_BASE
# are the per-service equivalents used by the seed scripts.

# Exercise a not-yet-seeded MCP locally without touching the shared DB:
# a JSON array of partial server rows (each with a `slug`), merged into the
# loaded catalog (lib/catalog.ts). EXTRA_MCP_ENDPOINTS does the same for
# planned endpoints (lib/endpoint-planner.ts).
# EXTRA_MCP_ROWS=
# EXTRA_MCP_ENDPOINTS=

# Local-only signing harness at /dev-workspace — 404s unless this is exactly
# '1' (app/dev-workspace/page.tsx). Never set it in production.
# DEV_WORKSPACE=1

# House-inference caps (lib/billing.ts) and the default inference slug.
# FREE_DAILY_TURN_CAP=40
# HOUSE_DAILY_TURN_CAP=2000
# DEFAULT_INFERENCE_SLUG=chatgpt

# Pinned router allowlists — comma-separated addresses that override the
# built-in LiFi router pins (lib/lifi-venue.ts, lib/lifi-bridge.ts).
# LIFI_ROUTERS=
# LIFI_BRIDGE_ROUTERS=

# Launchpad (x402-launch) — the MCP token factory. Defaults target Base
# Sepolia with a pinned factory; override per environment
# (lib/launch-contracts.ts, lib/launch-fees.ts).
# NEXT_PUBLIC_LAUNCH_CHAIN=base
# NEXT_PUBLIC_LAUNCH_FACTORY=0xYOUR_FACTORY
# LAUNCH_CHAIN=base
# LAUNCH_RPC_URL=
# LAUNCH_USDC=
# LAUNCH_FEE_ROUTER=
# LAUNCH_FEE_SHARE_BPS=


# ── Running the harness ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# `npm run test:api` drives the roster, tryouts, storefront, desk and cron
# surfaces, so a checkout missing these produces ~40 reds that read like
# regressions rather than missing config:
#
#   ROSTER_ENABLED=true, NEXT_PUBLIC_ROSTER_ENABLED=true,
#   BROKER_DESK_ENABLED=true, GUARDIAN_KEY_SECRET, HOUSE_MANAGER_KEY,
#   ADMIN_WALLETS, CRON_SECRET, OPENSEA_API_KEY, NEXT_PUBLIC_WC_PROJECT_ID
#
# NEXT_PUBLIC_* bakes in at BUILD time — rebuild after topping up, and run the
# harness against `next start` (a production build), never the dev server.
